   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "When defining the attributes of your data use factor() to specify the order of the levels. <div><br></div><div>?factor()</div><div><br></div><div>spiders$site&lt;-factor(spiders$site, levels=c(&quot;site1&quot;, &quot;site2&quot;, etc...)<br>\r\n\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Oct 4, 2012 at 8:05 PM, Sarah Loboda <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sarah....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\nHi,<div>I&#39;m new with R and newer with ggplot. I made a barplot with ggplot of my richness in function of my sites and habitat. </div><div><br></div><div>My data : </div><div>12 sites, 2 habitats (mesic and wet) in each site for a total of 24 observations. First column is my sites, second is my habitat and the last column is richness. </div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"240\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:180pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"80\" span=\"3\" style=\"width:60pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"80\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt;width:60pt\">site</td>\r\n  <td width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">habitat</td>\r\n  <td width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">richness</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">HAZ</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">7</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">HAZ</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">8</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">BAN</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">13</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">BAN</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">14</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">IQA</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">10</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">IQA</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">19</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">CB</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">12</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">CB</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">17</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">CHU</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">45</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">CHU</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">60</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">KUG</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">27</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">KUG</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">30</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">SCH</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">75</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">SCH</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">75</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">TOM</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">32</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">TOM</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">43</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">YEL</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">63</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">YEL</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">80</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">GB</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">51</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">GB</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">48</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">MOO</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">65</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">MOO</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">75</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">NW</td>\r\n  <td>mesic</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">80</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">NW</td>\r\n  <td>wet</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">109</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div>My code : </div><div><div>g&lt;-ggplot(spiders,aes(x=site,y=richness,fill=habitat))+ opts(title = &quot;Richness&quot;)</div><div>g + geom_bar(stat=&quot;identity&quot;, position=&quot;dodge&quot;)</div>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>I have something nice, almost what I wanted but I don&#39;t want my sites to be organized by alphabatical order. When I did a boxplot in R, I used the argument &quot;at&quot; to re-organise my boxes. Is there an equivalent of &quot;at&quot; for ggplot? The only page I could find on internet that was on this subject is not understandable for me : <a href=\"http://rstudio-pubs-static.s3.amazonaws.com/648_7f8e12b1f4b64f8086d90a5154ab197d.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio-pubs-static.s3.amazonaws.com/648_7f8e12b1f4b64f8086d90a5154ab197d.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374453816000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Pb_bKr4iaUAXjNSVPKbQx\">http://rstudio-pubs-static.s3.amazonaws.com/648_7f8e12b1f4b64f8086d90a5154ab197d.html</a> . Do you have a translation? </div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot :D</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374453816000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1KuXc8B_IEPBoWM7OIhziz\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374453816000&amp;usg=AOvVaw193mtRrwO2C86dscte68-b\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
